{
  "requirement": "`model` names the model on the Ollama server. The endpoint, credentials, and inference options configure requests to that server.\n\n```rust,ignore\n#[non_exhaustive]\npub struct OllamaConfig {\n    pub model: String,\n    pub endpoint: Option<String>,\n    pub api_key_env: Option<String>,\n    pub api_key: Option<SecretString>,\n    pub options: BTreeMap<String, OptionValue>,\n}\n\nimpl OllamaConfig {\n    pub fn new(model: String) -> Self;\n    pub fn endpoint(self, endpoint: String) -> Self;\n    pub fn api_key_env(self, api_key_env: String) -> Self;\n    pub fn api_key(self, api_key: SecretString) -> Self;\n    pub fn option(self, key: String, value: OptionValue) -> Self;\n}\n```\n\nTrait implementations\n\n```rust,ignore\nimpl Clone for OllamaConfig;\nimpl Debug for OllamaConfig;\nimpl<'de> Deserialize<'de> for OllamaConfig;\nimpl PartialEq for OllamaConfig;\nimpl Serialize for OllamaConfig;\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The tests cover each obligation in `requirements.sdk.graph.agent-harness.OllamaConfig`.\n\n- **Constructor and builders.** `mod[tests]/fn[backend_builders_set_only_the_requested_fields]` in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/config.rs` checks `OllamaConfig::new` serializes to only `{model}`. It then chains `endpoint`, `api_key_env`, `api_key` and `option`, and asserts every field serializes as set. A repeated `option` key overwrites the earlier value, and the model is preserved.\n- **Serde and PartialEq.** `fn[all_backends_preserve_nested_settings_and_credentials]` deserializes an ollama `AgentConfig` that has `api_key_env` and options. It asserts the serialized JSON matches the input, and that a string round trip gives an equal value.\n- **Defaults and credentials.** `fn[option_defaults_and_credential_resolution_are_deterministic]` covers the Ollama defaults and credentials.\n  - The default endpoint is `http://localhost:11434`, and with no key the resolved key is `None`.\n  - A missing `api_key_env` produces an error that names the variable.\n  - An explicit `api_key` is used even when the env name is absent.\n  - Non-finite option values are rejected in `options_json`.\n  - The `credential` helper handles env present, env empty, env missing, and explicit key.\n- **Requests to the server.** `supplied_ollama_backend_delivers_tools_and_results_over_native_chat` in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/configured.rs` runs a real local server. It confirms the configured model, the custom endpoint, the bearer `api_key`, and the `options` (`num_predict`) all reach the native `/api/chat` requests. This matches the statement that these fields configure requests to that server.\n- **Public shape.** `public_exports_match_the_appendix` in `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/public_api.rs` checks the public export inventory.\n\nThe `Clone` and `Debug` impls are plain derives with no logic of their own, so they need no dedicated tests. `PartialEq` is exercised by the equality assertions above. A successful lookup of a set `api_key_env` variable would need process-wide environment state. The shared `credential` helper is tested with an injected lookup instead, so I found no gap.",
  "references": "174253767003e4b5cd9421c1a9299b025ef99ddf813521a482831ecbbfc91c05",
